 "preregistered": {
  "estimators": "Per state and patch: the raw score mean with an empirical-Bernstein 95% interval (Maurer-Pontil Theorem 4, range 1, unbiased sample variance, two-sided) and the kernel-outcome fraction (z2 = -1 and t = +1) with a Wilson 95% interval; a readout-corrected score from the tensor product of single-qubit assignment matrices built from the readout pairing of the witness's batch, reported beside the raw value without an interval.",
  "contraction": "Under a depolarizing contraction V of the (q3, q1, q0) parity, kernel and bright states read (1 - V)/2 and (1 + V)/2, so kernel + bright - 1 is consistent with zero for each partner pair (k_i, b_i) and pooled over the four pairs, and middle and sector states read 1/2. A violation at |z| >= 3 on any such statistic of a patch names an error outside the contraction (readout bias, leakage or a coherent preparation error). Each z divides the raw residual by the square root of the summed sample variances over shots.",
  "pooling": "Patches are analyzed separately; the pooled value is the equal-weight mean over the three patches of the per-patch pooled kernel + bright - 1.",
  "stop_conditions": "Batch 0's readout reference shows a patch qubit with P(1|0) or P(0|1) above 0.15: stop and redraw the placement. A job fails or returns fewer shots than requested. The account-wide pause or the three-circuit limit would be broken."
 },
